  "mathematical_review": {
    "four_missing_counts": "The seven-type classification and arithmetic are valid and match the prior source review. Mixed-parity missing positions reduce each restricted profile to at most three unknown observations. For one parity, inverse evaluation at antipodes gives one of the 87 matrix classes. The 508-count and known-parity 252-count deductions are correct.",
    "conditional_eight_counts": "For missing points with no distance-eight pair, every off-diagonal antipodal coefficient is in {0,-10,8,-16}. Ternary RHS and parity force zero RHS. Choosing the largest absolute exceptional count M yields 128M <= 16(k-1)M <= 112M for k<=8. The argument permits mixed parity and handles the empty missing set by injectivity.",
    "sharpness": "The nine neighbours of a vertex have pairwise distance two. Empty versus singleton selections agree off those neighbours. Their nine-row antipodal matrix is 144I-16J and annihilates the all-ones vector. Thus the conditional threshold eight is sharp.",
    "coverage_and_arithmetic": "Native weak-composition enumeration gives 1149 valid ordered descriptions, 105 point-set orbits and 87 metric classes. Direct enumeration independently confirms the same 87 metrics from 2731135 triples. All 87 unbounded integer matrix implications have accepted kernel receipts.",
    "current_and_historical_status": "Earlier 238 support bounds are labelled as the state at that stage and linked to the new four-count section. Both manuscripts retain the unchanged 191--231 snake interval. No longer snake, global-bound improvement or novelty claim is made.",
    "next_step_6435": {
      "count": 6435,
      "proof": "A possible five-supported profile has one parity, since a mixed-parity split has parts of size at most four. It contains a distance-eight pair by the conditional theorem. Translation and a coordinate permutation send this pair to 0 and 255. On the first eight coordinates the other three ordered vertices have eight possible column patterns; their nonnegative multiplicities sum to eight, giving C(15,7)=6435 descriptions. For each vertex the ninth bit is uniquely determined by even parity. A common permutation of the first eight coordinates fixes both normalized endpoints, proving coverage. Removing repeated vertices preserves all five-distinct-position cases.",
      "scope": "A complete proposed description cover, not 6435 distinct isometry classes and not a completed five-support search.",
      "singular_case": "The proposal correctly retains singular matrices for separate bounded analysis and requires full-cube inverse validation of any arithmetic survivor."
    }
  },
